---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { pageMeta, reviewedOn } from "../data/seo";
---

<BaseLayout {...pageMeta.privacy} dateModified={reviewedOn}>
  <main class="subpage legal-page">
    <section class="subpage-hero">
      <p class="subpage-hero__path">Downright / Privacy</p>
      <h1>Local use is the default.</h1>
      <p>Downright does not need an account or cloud sync. The core app does not upload your Markdown or collect analytics. This site uses Vercel Web Analytics to measure anonymous page views; it does not use cookies.</p>
    </section>
    <article class="legal-copy">
      <h2>Files stay local</h2>
      <p>Read, edit, save, search, compare, watch, and export Markdown without a network connection. Open document text stays in the file you chose and in memory while you work.</p>
      <h2>Optional intelligence</h2>
      <p>Apple Intelligence is optional, on-device, and off by default. A user action starts each task. Downright 1.0 has no remote model integration.</p>
      <h2>Clear boundaries</h2>
      <p>Quick Look receives only the file Finder requests. Downright does not scan unrelated folders in the background. Snapshots, settings, and themes are local and user-controlled.</p>
      <h2>Site analytics</h2>
      <p>The site sends anonymized page-view data to Vercel Web Analytics. Vercel says Web Analytics does not use cookies and is available from the project dashboard. Analytics collection can be disabled by removing the site integration.</p>
      <p class="legal-copy__source">Source: <a href="https://github.com/ezzy1630/Downright/blob/main/Docs/PRIVACY.md">Docs/PRIVACY.md</a></p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
